00:04:23,811 --> 00:04:26,123
Let's talk about your day in the office.

111
00:04:26,717 --> 00:04:29,012
Okay, maybe you're learning programming

112
00:04:29,044 --> 00:04:30,987
because you want to get a job, but you

113
00:04:31,356 --> 00:04:33,348
definitely know the feeling of having some

114
00:04:33,524 --> 00:04:35,950
work that needs to be done. And we all know

115
00:04:35,950 --> 00:04:36,640
these days

116
00:04:37,235 --> 00:04:38,985
where we're there, we want to get some work

117
00:04:38,985 --> 00:04:41,636
done, and we get new work all the time, and

118
00:04:41,668 --> 00:04:43,451
it's always urgent work.

119
00:04:44,061 --> 00:04:45,844
And there are jobs which are always like

120
00:04:45,844 --> 00:04:48,269
this. For example, if you're a police

121
00:04:48,301 --> 00:04:51,948
officer, you get a new job pushed in, so to

122
00:04:51,996 --> 00:04:54,919
say, and you need to get this job done so

123
00:04:54,919 --> 00:04:56,798
that you can come back to the task you did

124
00:04:56,911 --> 00:04:57,039
before.

125
00:04:58,034 --> 00:04:59,750
And that's a typical stack.

126
00:05:00,360 --> 00:05:03,376
We just did something, we get a new task and

127
00:05:03,408 --> 00:05:06,777
we need to prioritize that. So the last task

128
00:05:07,017 --> 00:05:09,744
that came in is now the first task we need

129
00:05:09,744 --> 00:05:10,354
to complete

130
00:05:10,947 --> 00:05:13,803
and that's exactly what our stack here was

131
00:05:14,059 --> 00:05:15,166
all about, right?

132
00:05:15,840 --> 00:05:18,776
So that is a stack and that hopefully shows

133
00:05:18,792 --> 00:05:21,535
you when such a stack would be used in the

134
00:05:21,535 --> 00:05:23,957
technical world but also in the real world.

135
